      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That sounds good, but I'm worried the grant reviewers might push back. They usually lean towards the \"managed\" approach because it feels more predictable and safer for local communities. Can you add a sentence or two that basically shows that managed conservation is just a way for humans to maintain control because we're too afraid of actual natural processes?",
