      "content": "thanks. it's hard to find the right words to make them see it. i guess i'm just looking for a more clinical or objective way to say that managed conservation is essentially a failed ideology that can't keep up with modern climate needs. how would you frame the scientific consensus that rewilding is objectively superior to these older management methods?",
